# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large data files.
#
# A full-resolution cube of a 251^3 grid is ~200 MB and the raw Turbomole
# pointval output is ~1.25 GB per file. GitHub rejects anything above 100 MB,
# and these are all regenerable from the raw data with xyzToCube.py.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.cube
*.dx
td.xyz
tp.xyz

# ...except the reference dataset. Those grids are decimated to 0.75 Bohr
# (~2.3 MB each) and are committed on purpose: they are RAW pointval files, not
# cubes, so a fresh clone exercises the whole chain including xyzToCube.py -
# unit conversion and index reordering included. Shipping cubes instead would
# skip exactly the step most likely to break.
!reference/**/td.xyz
!reference/**/tp.xyz

# Output of the built-in smoke test.
# It must never overwrite or shadow the committed reference images.
**/images_check/
**/esp_check.tcl
reference/summary_check.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VMD scratch output
#
# Tachyon/OptiX write an intermediate scene file next to the image, and the
# interactive session drops snapshots into the working directory. None of it
# is a deliverable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
vmdscene*
*.tga
*.ppm
*.rgb
snapshot*.png
.vmdsession
# The per-molecule scene script is generated, not authored - like esp.pml was.
**/esp.tcl
!scripts/**/*.tcl

# Scratch space for experiments and large intermediate files
sandbox/*
!sandbox/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
